<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Amaprop half yr shr plunges, div steady.</title>
<headline>Amaprop half yr shr plunges, div steady.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Sept 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, after exceps (cts)   14.47   vs  36.50</p>
<p>    Shr, headline (cts)	 24.25   vs  36.60</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		     10.00   vs  10.00</p>
<p>    Attrib income		  7.35   vs  17.68</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			  8.68   vs  21.18</p>
<p>    Tax				4.36   vs   4.87</p>
<p>    Interest paid		 12.76   vs  15.06</p>
<p>    Turnover		     118.99   vs 138.79</p>
<p>Div payable Nov 29</p>
<p>on register Nov 22</p>
<p>Full name: Anglo American Properties Ltd</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	    4.97   vs  -</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it had resolved to award capitalisation shares to ordinary shareholders. Shareholders may elect instead to receive a cash dividend.</p>
<p>Amaprop said the profits before exceptional items for the second half of the year were expected to be slightly better than those achieved in the first half.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
